{%- comment -%}
  Renders the cart totals breakdown.
  Accepts:
  - context: {String} 'drawer' | 'main'
      'drawer' — one summary card: a collapsed total handle over the ledger
      'main'   — fully expanded: items subtotal, savings, divider, Total
  - section: {Object} the calling section. Drawer context only, and only
      `prepaid_banner_enabled` / `prepaid_banner_text` are read. Omit it and the
      prepaid row simply does not render.

  Usage:
  {% render 'cart-totals', context: 'main' %}
  {% render 'cart-totals', context: 'drawer', section: section %}
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign context = context | default: 'main'
  comment
    Derive this from money actually saved, not from the presence of a discount
    application. An application can allocate ₹0 (an app discount that matched
    nothing, a tier that rounds away), and keying off `.size > 0` then rendered an
    empty <ul> — in the drawer, a Total row that expands to a breakdown containing
    nothing but "Items subtotal".
  endcomment
  assign cart_total_saved = cart.original_total_price | minus: cart.total_price
  assign has_savings = false
  if cart_total_saved > 0
    assign has_savings = true
  endif

  comment
    Delivery is not an unknown by the time someone is looking at the cart: it is
    free above a threshold the theme already knows, tested against the
    POST-discount total, exactly as the shipping rate is configured. So it gets a
    row in the ledger with a real value, and the drawer no longer needs a separate
    celebration band saying the same thing 500px away from the total.
  endcomment
  assign ct_free_min = settings.free_shipping_minimum | default: 500 | times: 100
  assign ct_free_delivery = false
  if ct_free_min > 0 and cart.total_price >= ct_free_min
    assign ct_free_delivery = true
  endif

  comment
    The prepaid discount is applied by Razorpay at checkout, not by Shopify in the
    cart, so its amount genuinely is not known here. It gets a row that says so
    rather than a number, and it is NEVER subtracted from the total — a cart that
    quotes a figure the customer is not charged is worse than one that quotes
    nothing.
  endcomment
  assign ct_prepaid = false
  if context == 'drawer' and section.settings.prepaid_banner_enabled and section.settings.prepaid_banner_text != blank
    assign ct_prepaid = true
  endif

  assign ct_items_label = 'item'
  if cart.item_count != 1
    assign ct_items_label = 'items'
  endif
-%}

<div class="cart-totals cart-totals--{{ context }}">
  {%- if context == 'drawer' -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      One money surface. Everything the drawer has to say about price lives in
      this card and nowhere else — no discount pills on the cart lines, no
      separate free-delivery band, no reward totals. The breakdown is CLOSED by
      default: most shoppers never open it, and the ones who do get the whole
      ledger, down to the row that admits what is still unknown.

      The whole bar is the control, and the chevron sits with the label rather
      than beside the amount, so the affordance and the number do not compete.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      <cart-summary> only smooths the CLOSE. Opening already animates, because
      the browser sets `open` and then paints; closing does not, because it
      unsets `open` and the content stops being rendered in the same frame, so
      the height transition has nothing to run on. The element defers that unset
      until the transition finishes. With no JS it is still a working
      <details> — it just snaps shut, exactly as it does today.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <cart-summary class="cart-summary" data-cart-summary>
      <details class="cart-summary__d">
        <summary class="cart-summary__bar">
          <span class="cart-summary__k">
            <span class="cart-summary__lbl">
              Total to pay
              <span class="cart-summary__count">· {{ cart.item_count }} {{ ct_items_label }}</span>
              <span class="cart-summary__chevron" aria-hidden="true">{% render 'icon', icon: 'chevron-down' %}</span>
              {%- comment -%}
                An aria-label here would REPLACE the accessible name, so the row
                would announce the toggle and never the total it carries. The
                hint goes inside the name instead.
              {%- endcomment -%}
              <span class="sr-only">— show price breakdown</span>
            </span>
            {%- if has_savings or ct_free_delivery -%}
              <span class="cart-summary__save">
                {%- if has_savings -%}
                  You save {% render 'money-display', amount: cart_total_saved %}
                {%- endif -%}
                {%- if has_savings and ct_free_delivery -%}
                  <span class="cart-summary__dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                {%- endif -%}
                {%- if ct_free_delivery -%}Free delivery{%- endif -%}
              </span>
            {%- endif -%}
          </span>
          <span class="cart-summary__amt">{% render 'money-display', amount: cart.total_price, style: 'with_currency' %}</span>
        </summary>
        <div class="cart-summary__wrap">
          <div class="cart-summary__inner">
            <ul class="cart-summary__list list-unstyled" role="list">
              <li class="cart-summary__row">
                <span class="cart-summary__rk">{{ cart.item_count }} {{ ct_items_label }}</span>
                <span class="cart-summary__rv">{% render 'money-display', amount: cart.original_total_price %}</span>
              </li>
              {%- if has_savings -%}
                {%- render 'cart-savings-rows', style: 'ledger' -%}
              {%- endif -%}
              <li class="cart-summary__row">
                <span class="cart-summary__rk">Delivery</span>
                <span class="cart-summary__rv">
                  {%- if ct_free_delivery -%}Free{%- else -%}Calculated at checkout{%- endif -%}
                </span>
              </li>
              {%- if ct_prepaid -%}
                <li class="cart-summary__row cart-summary__row--soon">
                  <span class="cart-summary__rk">Prepaid discount</span>
                  <span class="cart-summary__rv">Applied at checkout</span>
                </li>
              {%- endif -%}
              <li class="cart-summary__row cart-summary__row--pay">
                <span class="cart-summary__rk">Total to pay</span>
                <span class="cart-summary__rv">{% render 'money-display', amount: cart.total_price, style: 'with_currency' %}</span>
              </li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </details>
      {%- if ct_prepaid -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          Outside the <details> on purpose: moving people off COD is worth a line
          of its own, so the nudge stays readable while the ledger is folded away.
          It sits inside the card, so it is still part of the one money surface.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <p class="cart-summary__prep">
          <span class="cart-summary__prep-icon" aria-hidden="true">{% render 'icon', icon: 'discount', size: 'sm' %}</span>
          {{ section.settings.prepaid_banner_text }}
        </p>
      {%- endif -%}
    </cart-summary>
  {%- else -%}
    <div class="cart-totals__row">
      <span class="cart-totals__label">Items subtotal</span>
      <span class="cart-totals__value">{% render 'money-display', amount: cart.original_total_price %}</span>
    </div>
    {%- if has_savings -%}
      <ul class="cart-totals__savings list-unstyled" role="list" aria-label="{{ 'customer.order.discount' | t | escape }}">
        {%- render 'cart-savings-rows' -%}
      </ul>
    {%- endif -%}
    <hr class="cart-totals__divider" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="cart-totals__row cart-totals__grand-total">
      <span class="cart-totals__label">Total</span>
      <span class="cart-totals__value">{% render 'money-display', amount: cart.total_price, style: 'with_currency' %}</span>
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- liquid
    comment
      When delivery is free there is no tax note AT ALL any more — not
      "calculated at checkout" (wrongly implied one more number was coming on
      MRP-priced garments), and as of now not "Including all Taxes" either:
      the ledger and the button already agree on one final figure, and a
      caveat line under a checkout button is one more thing to read between
      the shopper and the tap. The non-free-delivery branches keep their
      stock wording, where shipping genuinely is still open.
    endcomment
    assign ct_hide_note = false
    if ct_free_delivery
      assign ct_hide_note = true
    endif
  -%}
  {%- unless ct_hide_note -%}
    <div class="cart-totals__note tax-note text-opacity text-2sm rte">
      {%- liquid
        if cart.taxes_included and shop.shipping_policy.body != blank
          echo 'cart.general.taxes_included_and_shipping_policy_html' | t: link: shop.shipping_policy.url
        elsif cart.taxes_included
          echo 'cart.general.taxes_included_but_shipping_at_checkout' | t
        elsif shop.shipping_policy.body != blank
          echo 'cart.general.taxes_and_shipping_policy_at_checkout_html' | t: link: shop.shipping_policy.url
        else
          echo 'cart.general.taxes_and_shipping_at_checkout' | t
        endif
      -%}
    </div>
  {%- endunless -%}
</div>
